WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.847
The lag function is useful when the question includes words such as previous, change, or time since.

00:00:07.847 --> 00:00:14.397
Lag looks backward in an ordered sequence and brings an earlier value onto the current row.

00:00:14.977 --> 00:00:22.831
For example, for each patient admission, we can bring the previous discharge date beside the current admission date.

00:00:22.831 --> 00:00:26.776
The partition defines whose history we are following.

00:00:26.776 --> 00:00:29.961
The order defines what previous means.

00:00:29.961 --> 00:00:35.393
Without a meaningful partition and order, lag cannot answer the question correctly.
